# decision-emission enforcement sentinel — read by deploy.sh
# cmd_check_decision_emission (--check-decision-emission, Check 61).
#
# First non-comment token decides whether an INCOMPLETE verdict BLOCKS:
#   enforce  -> INCOMPLETE exits 1 (blocking)
#   warn     -> INCOMPLETE reports the true verdict, exits 0 (non-blocking)
#
# Ships `warn`. The `shadow` rung of the shadow -> warn -> enforce ladder
# (progressive-rollout-convention.md) is NOT reachable in this codebase —
# resolve_check_mode() accepts enforce|warn|off only — so this gate enters at
# the lowest IMPLEMENTABLE rung and walks warn -> enforce -> removed. Recorded
# explicitly rather than silently skipped.
#
# The flip to `enforce` is an OPERATOR DECISION, never auto-promoted by hit
# count (progressive-rollout-convention.md, verbatim). The flip ledger lives in
# core/standards/gate-efficacy-standard.md § Flip-decision status.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GRADUATION CLAUSE — read this before flipping the token below.
#
# Check 61's predicate is SPLIT BY LOCUS OF INPUT (ADR-166), and this sentinel
# governs ONLY ONE OF THE TWO HALVES. Flipping it is not the whole graduation,
# and on its own it changes nothing observable in CI.
#
#   STEP 1 — flip the token below to `enforce`.
#     This arms the LIVE ARM only: an INCOMPLETE/NOSET verdict then exits 1
#     instead of 0. In CI it does NOTHING, because the live arm's verdict input
#     is the pipeline event log — git-ignored operator-instance state, absent
#     from every checkout — so the CI run verdicts SKIP and exits 3 either way.
#     SKIP is sentinel-AGNOSTIC on purpose: mapping it to 1 under enforce would
#     turn this flip into a permanent red on every pull request rather than into
#     enforcement. The live arm's real surface is deploy time and Stage-13
#     close-out, where the event log exists.
#
#   STEP 2 — register the MACHINERY ARM's context in branch protection.
#     Context name: "Decision-emission gate integrity (Check 61 machinery)",
#     from .github/workflows/decision-emission.yml. This is a repository-settings
#     action a pull request structurally CANNOT perform, so it is an operator
#     step taken outside any PR. That arm reads no sentinel and honours none —
#     it is red-capable today — so registration is the only thing standing
#     between it and `required`.
#
#   THERE IS NO STEP 3, and saying so is the point. The sibling
#   close-completeness.enforce clause carries a delete-the-paths-filter step;
#   this gate has none, because decision-emission.yml ships FILTER-FREE
#   (`always-reports=yes` is a prerequisite for any `required` trajectory, not a
#   later optimization). A graduation clause that silently omits a step is how a
#   flip half-lands, so the absence is stated rather than left to be inferred.
#
#   WHAT NEITHER STEP ACHIEVES. Registering the machinery arm does not make the
#   emission RECORD a required check — only the machinery that would detect a
#   gap in it. The live half is a PERMANENT advisory residual: its verdict-input
#   closure over repository paths is empty, so `required` is structurally
#   unavailable to it rather than pending. Do not read a green machinery context
#   as the backlog-resident claim.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
warn
